t the number  running  wild the plan seems to be working well  and frankie plans to make hotshot regret  treating the great general frankie like  a toy  although you gotta admit he does look  like a toy albeit  a really epic one zorro andre keep  fighting since zoro doesn't really trust  him yet  but as apu is trying to call more  numbers we get to see these two cool  characters team up against him  building some trust there and it's nice  to see apu scrambling and in trouble  and as if we needed more reasons to like  drake he also says that he hated abu  since the beginning  and that he's gonna crush him for his  own sake zoro agrees and we seem to have  a growing understanding between these  two now  and i really do like the alliance  between these two supernovas  specifically but it can't be that easy  apu keeps getting lucky and  queen straight up starts firing bullets  from a machine gun  suggesting that drake shouldn't for a  second think that he'll be allowed to  escape  he calls him a traitor and then corrects  himself to spy  since he wasn't truly loyal to kaido  from the beginning at first drake seems  unfazed  wondering why queen would think bullets  would hurt him but then he wonders about  the bullet  suggesting that there could be more to  it it could contain  sea stone or could be poisoned since  biological warfare  would definitely not be a surprise for  kaido's crew at this point  whatever it is they're not normal  bullets we can rest assured of that  and queen knows what he's doing on the  roof we straight up see an all-star  namely  jack getting his tusk cut off and he  falls  clearly overpowered by his opponents he  looks straight up defeated which is a  shock to me in the sense that i thought  the fight would be shown more on screen  and not just the end result by doing it  this way oda seems to be hyping up the  power of sulong nekomamushi and  inuarashi even more  as if he's saying the fight wasn't even  close so why bother showing it  now i'm all the more hyped to see these  two in action  the point is though even without luffy  there yet  our samurai are doing well really well  kaido straight up says that jack is  all-star and his precious men  are being killed jack apologizes to  kaido but kaido explains it's not  because he's weak  it's because the tsulong inuarashi and  nekomamushi are just way too  strong which is so hype coming from  iyanko  what's interesting is how much kaido is  recognizing the strength of his opponent  and how caring and understanding he  seems to be concerning his men here i  love learning about kaido because there  always seems to be more that meets the  eye with him  he clearly isn't just a survival of the  fittest if you lose you die kind of  leader  he actually calls his men precious and  he comforts jack  very interesting stuff and he definitely  seems like a better leader  now than i expected him to be at first  yeah jack  will probably get up again at some point  but i don't see him being much of a  threat moving forward  and that's saying a lot since he's  supposed to be one of kaido's strongest  men kaido lets us know that the sulong  plan  was effective and they caused a lot of  damage  but they couldn't do more than that and  then he tells jack to go heal up  implying that he'll be just fine long  term kinemon then thanks the mink  warriors  and then goes on to straight up cut  through kaido's heat blast  and when he was first introduced as a  fire cutter who would have thought  that he'd go on to use it so effectively  and epically  against a yonko of all people this  moment is definitely the pinnacle of  such an ability and i believe oda  handled it very nicely here  he appears to hit kaido with his slash  to the yonko's shock  again kaido is showing significant  vulnerability before luffy and the  others have even showed up the samurai  make it clear  that they're not looking to escape from  kaido they want to die here as  lord odin samurai and they will take  k